From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@zoho.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:02:23 +0300
Subject: Legacy renderer: minimap render target power-of-two sized, skipped
 when hidden; no crash when render to texture failed

GL1RenderTarget's destructor dereferenced its texture, which is NULL when
the FBO could not be made ("GL1RenderTarget: Cannot render to texture"):
the game crashed with SIGSEGV when the race ended. Check it first.

The minimap is rendered once per race into an FBO colour texture with a
depth renderbuffer of twice the minimap's size, which is not a power of
two (810x810 at 1080p): with the legacy renderer use the largest power of
two not above it (512x512), the size old GPUs render to natively and less
memory; the minimap coordinates already scale with the texture's size.
When the minimap is hidden (Minimap display="2") nothing draws it, so it
isn't rendered at all.

diff --git a/src/graphics/render_target.cpp b/src/graphics/render_target.cpp
--- a/src/graphics/render_target.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/render_target.cpp
@@ -51,8 +51,10 @@ GL1RenderTarget::GL1RenderTarget(const irr::core::dimension2du &dimension,
 
 GL1RenderTarget::~GL1RenderTarget()
 {
-    // GE doesn't add rtt texture to cache
-    if (m_render_target_texture->getDriverType() == video::EDT_VULKAN)
+    // GE doesn't add rtt texture to cache. NULL when render to texture
+    // failed (the destructor dereferenced it: a crash when the race ended)
+    if (m_render_target_texture != NULL &&
+        m_render_target_texture->getDriverType() == video::EDT_VULKAN)
         m_render_target_texture->drop();
 }
 
diff --git a/src/tracks/track.cpp b/src/tracks/track.cpp
--- a/src/tracks/track.cpp
+++ b/src/tracks/track.cpp
@@ -1230,11 +1230,32 @@ void Track::loadMinimap()
     if (GUIEngine::isNoGraphics())
         return;
 
+    // A hidden minimap is never drawn (RaceGUI): don't render it at all,
+    // which saves its colour texture and depth buffer (the overworld draws
+    // its map whatever the setting)
+    if (UserConfigParams::m_minimap_display == 2 &&
+        RaceManager::get()->getMinorMode() !=
+        RaceManager::MINOR_MODE_OVERWORLD)
+        return;
+
     //Create the minimap resizing it as necessary.
     core::dimension2du mini_map_size = World::getWorld()->getRaceGUI()->getMiniMapSize();
 
     //Use twice the size of the rendered minimap to reduce significantly aliasing
-    m_render_target = Graph::get()->makeMiniMap(mini_map_size * 2,
+    core::dimension2du rtt_size = mini_map_size * 2;
+    if (!CVS->isGLSL())
+    {
+        // The legacy renderer renders it into an FBO texture with a depth
+        // renderbuffer of the same size: keep both power-of-two sized (the
+        // largest not above the wanted size), which old GPUs such as nv30
+        // render to in their native (swizzled) layout, and smaller
+        unsigned pot = 64;
+        const unsigned want = std::min(rtt_size.Width, rtt_size.Height);
+        while (pot * 2 <= want)
+            pot *= 2;
+        rtt_size = core::dimension2du(pot, pot);
+    }
+    m_render_target = Graph::get()->makeMiniMap(rtt_size,
         "minimap::" + m_ident, video::SColor(127, 255, 255, 255),
         m_minimap_invert_x_z);
 
